window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b247-ba96dc00787a520a.json"]={sha256:"ba96dc00787a520ae3c5672b0fbecd014ec972fe5967025c465db42041977e4b",value:{"id":"b247","title":"側槽式溢洪道","titleEn":"Side-channel spillways","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以側向入流動量及沿程水面控制側槽為主線，先用沿程入流與累積與長堰流量與水頭界定水力與構造條件，再將出口臨界控制、波峰餘高與牆頂連結到模型守恆與驗證。側槽具有空間變流，示意分段平均不代替完整三維模型與沿程動量求解。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops controlling side channels through lateral inflow momentum and profiles through Lateral inflow accumulation and Long crest discharge and head, then connects Critical outlet control and Wave allowance and wall crest to Model conservation and validation. Side channels have spatially varied flow; segmented averages do not replace three-dimensional modeling and longitudinal momentum analysis. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["沿程入流與累積","Lateral inflow accumulation"],["側入動量與轉向","Lateral momentum and turning"],["出口臨界控制","Critical outlet control"],["波峰餘高與牆頂","Wave allowance and wall crest"],["模型守恆與驗證","Model conservation and validation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["沿程入流與累積","側入動量與轉向","出口臨界控制","波峰餘高與牆頂","模型守恆與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Lateral inflow accumulation","Lateral momentum and turning","Critical outlet control","Wave allowance and wall crest","Model conservation and validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查沿程入流與累積：Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s；再獨立檢查長堰流量與水頭：Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s。敏感度：均勻側入流由每公尺2增至3m2/s且側槽長40m時，總流量由80增至120m3/s；若出口面積維持20m2，平均速度由4增為6m/s，動量與能量需求不只增加50%。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。側槽具有空間變流，示意分段平均不代替完整三維模型與沿程動量求解。 將同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Lateral inflow accumulation: Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s. Independently examine Long crest discharge and head: Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s. Sensitivity: increasing uniform lateral inflow from2 to3m2/s along40m raises discharge from80 to120m3/s. At a fixed20m2 outlet area, velocity rises from4 to6m/s; momentum and energy demands grow faster than the50-percent discharge increase. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Side channels have spatially varied flow; segmented averages do not replace three-dimensional modeling and longitudinal momentum analysis. Use the following independent check: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b247-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「沿程入流與累積」與「長堰流量與水頭」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lateral inflow accumulation\" and \"Long crest discharge and head\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b247-v15-01","title":"沿程入流與累積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lateral inflow accumulation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「沿程入流與累積」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lateral inflow accumulation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側槽接收沿堰長分布的側向水流，流量沿下游增加，因此不能用一個固定流量套全槽。先把側入流分布積分，再檢查各段斷面與出口控制；堰上水頭不均或局部淹沒會破壞均勻入流假設。 驗證時應分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對，並辨識以下失效情境：局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沿程入流與累積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A side channel accumulates distributed lateral inflow, so discharge increases downstream. Integrate the inflow distribution before checking sections and outlet control rather than applying one discharge everywhere. Unequal crest heads or local submergence invalidate the uniform-inflow approximation and require segmented measurements. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lateral inflow accumulation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沿程入流與累積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lateral inflow accumulation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-01-k1","title":"沿程入流與累積","titleEn":"Lateral inflow accumulation","text":"側槽接收沿堰長分布的側向水流，流量沿下游增加，因此不能用一個固定流量套全槽。先把側入流分布積分，再檢查各段斷面與出口控制；堰上水頭不均或局部淹沒會破壞均勻入流假設。","textEn":"A side channel accumulates distributed lateral inflow, so discharge increases downstream. Integrate the inflow distribution before checking sections and outlet control rather than applying one discharge everywhere.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沿程入流與累積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral inflow accumulation\" is correct?","options":["側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同","側槽接收沿堰長分布的側向水流，流量沿下游增加，因此不能用一個固定流量套全槽。","堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量"],"optionsEn":["Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel","A side channel accumulates distributed lateral inflow, so discharge increases downstream.","Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"側槽接收沿堰長分布的側向水流，流量沿下游增加，因此不能用一個固定流量套全槽。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A side channel accumulates distributed lateral inflow, so discharge increases downstream. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b247-v15-02","title":"沿程入流與累積：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral inflow accumulation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沿程入流與累積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lateral inflow accumulation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沿程入流與累積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral inflow accumulation\", which statement holds?","options":["連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線","側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平","原創教學假設：Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s。"],"optionsEn":["Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile","The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section","Original teaching assumptions: Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Uniform lateral input=2 m2/s; channelLength=40 m; upstreamQ=0; outletQ=2*40=80 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b247-v15-03","title":"沿程入流與累積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral inflow accumulation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沿程入流與累積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lateral inflow accumulation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沿程入流與累積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral inflow accumulation\"?","options":["分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b247-v15-04","title":"沿程入流與累積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral inflow accumulation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沿程入流與累積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lateral inflow accumulation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配。診斷時應採取以下查核：分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配。診斷時應採取以下查核：分段量測堰上水頭並將側入流累積量與出口流量比對，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure crest head by segment and compare accumulated inflow with outlet discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沿程入流與累積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral inflow accumulation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配。","堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution.","Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部堰頂淹沒會改變沿程入流分配。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local crest submergence changes the longitudinal inflow distribution. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b247-v15-05","title":"長堰流量與水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Long crest discharge and head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「長堰流量與水頭」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long crest discharge and head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側槽可提供較長堰頂以降低特定流量所需水頭，但係數仍受入口形狀、接近流與淹沒控制。自由堰公式只適用所假設的係數與單位；堰長增加不保證出口通道有足夠容量，應聯合分析槽內回水。 驗證時應比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況，並辨識以下失效情境：只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「長堰流量與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A long crest can reduce the head needed for discharge, but coefficient, approach flow and submergence remain important. A free-weir equation applies only to its stated geometry and units. More crest length does not guarantee outlet capacity because channel backwater may suppress the intended inflow. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long crest discharge and head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「長堰流量與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Long crest discharge and head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-05-k1","title":"長堰流量與水頭","titleEn":"Long crest discharge and head","text":"側槽可提供較長堰頂以降低特定流量所需水頭，但係數仍受入口形狀、接近流與淹沒控制。自由堰公式只適用所假設的係數與單位；堰長增加不保證出口通道有足夠容量，應聯合分析槽內回水。","textEn":"A long crest can reduce the head needed for discharge, but coefficient, approach flow and submergence remain important. A free-weir equation applies only to its stated geometry and units.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長堰流量與水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long crest discharge and head\" is correct?","options":["堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量","側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量","側槽可提供較長堰頂以降低特定流量所需水頭，但係數仍受入口形狀、接近流與淹沒控制。"],"optionsEn":["Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit","Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel","A long crest can reduce the head needed for discharge, but coefficient, approach flow and submergence remain important."],"answer":2,"explanation":"側槽可提供較長堰頂以降低特定流量所需水頭，但係數仍受入口形狀、接近流與淹沒控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A long crest can reduce the head needed for discharge, but coefficient, approach flow and submergence remain important. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b247-v15-06","title":"長堰流量與水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Long crest discharge and head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長堰流量與水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long crest discharge and head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長堰流量與水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long crest discharge and head\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s。","出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游","平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s.","Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel","A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Assumed coefficient C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestLength=30 m; head=1.2 m; Q=1.7*30*1.2**1.5=67.0412 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b247-v15-07","title":"長堰流量與水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long crest discharge and head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長堰流量與水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long crest discharge and head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長堰流量與水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long crest discharge and head\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況。","堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence.","Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b247-v15-08","title":"長堰流量與水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long crest discharge and head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長堰流量與水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long crest discharge and head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較各堰段水頭與實測流量並標示淹沒工況，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare head and measured discharge for each crest segment and identify submergence. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長堰流量與水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long crest discharge and head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量","只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel","Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只增加堰長但不檢查側槽容量可能使堰頂回水淹沒。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing crest length without channel checks can submerge the crest through backwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b247-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「側入動量與轉向」與「斷面速度與水深」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lateral momentum and turning\" and \"Section velocity and depth\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b247-v15-09","title":"側入動量與轉向：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lateral momentum and turning: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「側入動量與轉向」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lateral momentum and turning” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"垂直於槽軸的側入流需轉向後才沿槽輸送，其軸向初始動量可能很小，不能使用只含能量損失的普通渠道公式忽略混合作用。控制體應包含各入口速度向量、壁面反力與壓力力，簡化動量差只展示其中一項。 驗證時應以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「側入動量與轉向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lateral inflow must turn into the channel axis and may carry little initial axial momentum. Ordinary channel calculations that only add an energy-loss coefficient can miss mixing forces. A control volume needs inlet velocity vectors, wall reactions and pressure forces; a simplified momentum difference illustrates only one contribution. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lateral momentum and turning” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「側入動量與轉向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lateral momentum and turning”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-09-k1","title":"側入動量與轉向","titleEn":"Lateral momentum and turning","text":"垂直於槽軸的側入流需轉向後才沿槽輸送，其軸向初始動量可能很小，不能使用只含能量損失的普通渠道公式忽略混合作用。控制體應包含各入口速度向量、壁面反力與壓力力，簡化動量差只展示其中一項。","textEn":"Lateral inflow must turn into the channel axis and may carry little initial axial momentum. Ordinary channel calculations that only add an energy-loss coefficient can miss mixing forces.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側入動量與轉向」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral momentum and turning\" is correct?","options":["垂直於槽軸的側入流需轉向後才沿槽輸送，其軸向初始動量可能很小，不能使用只含能量損失的普通渠道公式忽略混合作用。","側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量","連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線"],"optionsEn":["Lateral inflow must turn into the channel axis and may carry little initial axial momentum.","Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel","Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile"],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂直於槽軸的側入流需轉向後才沿槽輸送，其軸向初始動量可能很小，不能使用只含能量損失的普通渠道公式忽略混合作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lateral inflow must turn into the channel axis and may carry little initial axial momentum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b247-v15-10","title":"側入動量與轉向：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral momentum and turning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側入動量與轉向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lateral momentum and turning” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側入動量與轉向」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral momentum and turning\", which statement holds?","options":["側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN。","排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓"],"optionsEn":["The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN.","The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; axialOutflow=80 m3/s at4 m/s; lateral axial velocity=0; outgoingAxialMomentum=1000*80*4/1000=320 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b247-v15-11","title":"側入動量與轉向：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral momentum and turning: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側入動量與轉向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lateral momentum and turning” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側入動量與轉向」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral momentum and turning\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確","以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct","Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b247-v15-12","title":"側入動量與轉向：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral momentum and turning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側入動量與轉向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lateral momentum and turning” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力。診斷時應採取以下查核：以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力。診斷時應採取以下查核：以三維速度量測確認側入方向並核對控制體各面動量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure three-dimensional velocity and reconcile momentum across every control-volume face. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側入動量與轉向」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral momentum and turning\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile"],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略側向混合會誤判沿程水深與壁面反力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring lateral mixing misstates channel depth and wall reactions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b247-v15-13","title":"斷面速度與水深：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Section velocity and depth: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「斷面速度與水深」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Section velocity and depth” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側槽寬度和水深共同提供逐漸增加的通水面積，單純以平均速度限值配置寬度會漏掉回流與旋轉。連續方程可核對量測是否一致，但不能獨自決定水面線；需同時滿足動量、底坡與下游邊界。 驗證時應用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積，並辨識以下失效情境：把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「斷面速度與水深」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Width and depth provide area for increasing downstream flow. A mean-velocity target alone misses recirculation and rotation. Continuity checks whether measurements agree but cannot determine the water profile independently of momentum, bed slope and the downstream boundary; use it as one equation within the system. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Section velocity and depth” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「斷面速度與水深」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Section velocity and depth”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-13-k1","title":"斷面速度與水深","titleEn":"Section velocity and depth","text":"側槽寬度和水深共同提供逐漸增加的通水面積，單純以平均速度限值配置寬度會漏掉回流與旋轉。連續方程可核對量測是否一致，但不能獨自決定水面線；需同時滿足動量、底坡與下游邊界。","textEn":"Width and depth provide area for increasing downstream flow. A mean-velocity target alone misses recirculation and rotation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斷面速度與水深」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Section velocity and depth\" is correct?","options":["連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線","側槽寬度和水深共同提供逐漸增加的通水面積，單純以平均速度限值配置寬度會漏掉回流與旋轉。","出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游"],"optionsEn":["Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile","Width and depth provide area for increasing downstream flow.","Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"側槽寬度和水深共同提供逐漸增加的通水面積，單純以平均速度限值配置寬度會漏掉回流與旋轉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Width and depth provide area for increasing downstream flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b247-v15-14","title":"斷面速度與水深：定量估算","titleEn":"Section velocity and depth: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷面速度與水深」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Section velocity and depth” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斷面速度與水深」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Section velocity and depth\", which statement holds?","options":["平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流","堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同","原創教學假設：Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping","Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects","Original teaching assumptions: Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=90 m3/s; width=8 m; depth=3 m; meanV=90/(8*3)=3.75 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b247-v15-15","title":"斷面速度與水深：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Section velocity and depth: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷面速度與水深」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Section velocity and depth” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斷面速度與水深」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Section velocity and depth\"?","options":["用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b247-v15-16","title":"斷面速度與水深：失效診斷","titleEn":"Section velocity and depth: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷面速度與水深」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Section velocity and depth” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度。診斷時應採取以下查核：用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. Diagnose it by the following check: Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度。診斷時應採取以下查核：用分層流速剖面檢查平均速度及回流面積，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. Diagnose it by the following check: Use layered velocity profiles to check mean speed and recirculating area. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斷面速度與水深」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Section velocity and depth\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度。","出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity.","Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把回流區算成有效順流面積會低估主流速度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting recirculation as effective downstream area understates main-stream velocity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b247-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「出口臨界控制」與「橫向水位與彎流」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Critical outlet control\" and \"Transverse level and curved flow\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b247-v15-17","title":"出口臨界控制：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Critical outlet control: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「出口臨界控制」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Critical outlet control” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"出口收縮或跌水可能建立臨界控制並把回水影響傳回側槽，需將出口與側向堰頂聯合評估。矩形臨界深度只對指定單寬流量成立；若有含氣、斜交或非矩形斷面，需用適用水力深度及完整模型。 驗證時應量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移，並辨識以下失效情境：漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出口臨界控制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An outlet contraction or drop may impose critical control and send backwater upstream toward the lateral crest. Evaluate the outlet and side weir jointly. Rectangular critical depth applies to a specified unit discharge; aeration, oblique approach or different geometry requires a more suitable formulation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Critical outlet control” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出口臨界控制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Critical outlet control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-17-k1","title":"出口臨界控制","titleEn":"Critical outlet control","text":"出口收縮或跌水可能建立臨界控制並把回水影響傳回側槽，需將出口與側向堰頂聯合評估。矩形臨界深度只對指定單寬流量成立；若有含氣、斜交或非矩形斷面，需用適用水力深度及完整模型。","textEn":"An outlet contraction or drop may impose critical control and send backwater upstream toward the lateral crest. Evaluate the outlet and side weir jointly.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「出口臨界控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Critical outlet control\" is correct?","options":["出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游","側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平","出口收縮或跌水可能建立臨界控制並把回水影響傳回側槽，需將出口與側向堰頂聯合評估。"],"optionsEn":["Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel","The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section","An outlet contraction or drop may impose critical control and send backwater upstream toward the lateral crest."],"answer":2,"explanation":"出口收縮或跌水可能建立臨界控制並把回水影響傳回側槽，需將出口與側向堰頂聯合評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An outlet contraction or drop may impose critical control and send backwater upstream toward the lateral crest. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b247-v15-18","title":"出口臨界控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Critical outlet control: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出口臨界控制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Critical outlet control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「出口臨界控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Critical outlet control\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m。","排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓","水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m.","The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor","Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=80 m3/s; outletWidth=8 m; q=10 m2/s; criticalDepth=(10**2/9.81)**(1/3)=2.16825 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b247-v15-19","title":"出口臨界控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Critical outlet control: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出口臨界控制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Critical outlet control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「出口臨界控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Critical outlet control\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移。","堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge.","Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b247-v15-20","title":"出口臨界控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Critical outlet control: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出口臨界控制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Critical outlet control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測出口附近水面線並檢查控制斷面是否隨流量遷移，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure the outlet profile and determine whether the control section shifts with discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「出口臨界控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Critical outlet control\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平","漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section","Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏掉出口控制會低估側槽上游水位。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Missing outlet control underestimates upstream channel level. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b247-v15-21","title":"橫向水位與彎流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transverse level and curved flow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「橫向水位與彎流」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transverse level and curved flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側流轉向與彎道可使橫向水位傾斜，平均縱向水面線不能代表外側牆邊最高水位。曲率平衡簡式以均勻速度和大半徑近似，回流與湍流時只能提供量級；需分別觀測內外側水位與波峰。 驗證時應同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場，並辨識以下失效情境：只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橫向水位與彎流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Turning flow can tilt the transverse water surface, so a mean longitudinal profile does not capture the highest wall level. A curvature balance assumes approximately uniform velocity and gentle curvature; recirculating turbulent flow makes it only a scale estimate. Observe both banks and wave crests independently. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transverse level and curved flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橫向水位與彎流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transverse level and curved flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-21-k1","title":"橫向水位與彎流","titleEn":"Transverse level and curved flow","text":"側流轉向與彎道可使橫向水位傾斜，平均縱向水面線不能代表外側牆邊最高水位。曲率平衡簡式以均勻速度和大半徑近似，回流與湍流時只能提供量級；需分別觀測內外側水位與波峰。","textEn":"Turning flow can tilt the transverse water surface, so a mean longitudinal profile does not capture the highest wall level. A curvature balance assumes approximately uniform velocity and gentle curvature; recirculating turbulent flow makes it only a scale estimate.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橫向水位與彎流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transverse level and curved flow\" is correct?","options":["側流轉向與彎道可使橫向水位傾斜，平均縱向水面線不能代表外側牆邊最高水位。","側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平","平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流"],"optionsEn":["Turning flow can tilt the transverse water surface, so a mean longitudinal profile does not capture the highest wall level.","The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section","A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping"],"answer":0,"explanation":"側流轉向與彎道可使橫向水位傾斜，平均縱向水面線不能代表外側牆邊最高水位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Turning flow can tilt the transverse water surface, so a mean longitudinal profile does not capture the highest wall level. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b247-v15-22","title":"橫向水位與彎流：定量估算","titleEn":"Transverse level and curved flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橫向水位與彎流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transverse level and curved flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橫向水位與彎流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transverse level and curved flow\", which statement holds?","options":["堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同","原創教學假設：V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m。","側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects","Original teaching assumptions: V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m.","Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=4 m/s; width=6 m; curvatureRadius=30 m; levelDifference=4**2*6/(9.81*30)=0.326198 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b247-v15-23","title":"橫向水位與彎流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transverse level and curved flow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橫向水位與彎流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transverse level and curved flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橫向水位與彎流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transverse level and curved flow\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量","同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel","Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b247-v15-24","title":"橫向水位與彎流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transverse level and curved flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橫向水位與彎流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transverse level and curved flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測內外側水位與波峰並對照轉彎速度場，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure levels and crests at both walls simultaneously alongside turning velocities. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橫向水位與彎流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transverse level and curved flow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流"],"optionsEn":["A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只在內側設水位計會漏掉外側越流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A gauge only at the inner wall can miss outer-wall overtopping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b247-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「波峰餘高與牆頂」與「底板排水與回水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wave allowance and wall crest\" and \"Floor drainage and backwater\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b247-v15-25","title":"波峰餘高與牆頂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wave allowance and wall crest: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「波峰餘高與牆頂」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wave allowance and wall crest” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側入水舌的碰撞會產生交叉波與噴濺，牆頂核對需區分平均水深、波幅與測量不確定度。簡單加總只整理已選定工況的幾何餘量，不會自動提供完整可靠度；洪水歷線與短暫浪峰仍要在試驗中覆蓋。 驗證時應以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段，並辨識以下失效情境：時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波峰餘高與牆頂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Colliding lateral jets generate cross-waves and splash. Separate mean depth, wave amplitude and measurement uncertainty when checking a wall crest. A simple sum organizes geometry for an assumed case rather than establishing reliability; test hydrographs and short-lived crests as part of the boundary coverage. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave allowance and wall crest” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「波峰餘高與牆頂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave allowance and wall crest”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-25-k1","title":"波峰餘高與牆頂","titleEn":"Wave allowance and wall crest","text":"側入水舌的碰撞會產生交叉波與噴濺，牆頂核對需區分平均水深、波幅與測量不確定度。簡單加總只整理已選定工況的幾何餘量，不會自動提供完整可靠度；洪水歷線與短暫浪峰仍要在試驗中覆蓋。","textEn":"Colliding lateral jets generate cross-waves and splash. Separate mean depth, wave amplitude and measurement uncertainty when checking a wall crest.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波峰餘高與牆頂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wave allowance and wall crest\" is correct?","options":["平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流","側入水舌的碰撞會產生交叉波與噴濺，牆頂核對需區分平均水深、波幅與測量不確定度。","排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓"],"optionsEn":["A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping","Colliding lateral jets generate cross-waves and splash.","The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor"],"answer":1,"explanation":"側入水舌的碰撞會產生交叉波與噴濺，牆頂核對需區分平均水深、波幅與測量不確定度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Colliding lateral jets generate cross-waves and splash. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b247-v15-26","title":"波峰餘高與牆頂：定量估算","titleEn":"Wave allowance and wall crest: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波峰餘高與牆頂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wave allowance and wall crest” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波峰餘高與牆頂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wave allowance and wall crest\", which statement holds?","options":["水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確","堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量","原創教學假設：wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m。"],"optionsEn":["Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct","Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit","Original teaching assumptions: wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: wallHeight=5 m; meanDepth=3.6 m; waveCrestAboveMean=0.8 m; geometricClearance=5-3.6-0.8=0.60 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b247-v15-27","title":"波峰餘高與牆頂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wave allowance and wall crest: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「波峰餘高與牆頂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wave allowance and wall crest” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波峰餘高與牆頂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wave allowance and wall crest\"?","options":["以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線"],"optionsEn":["Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b247-v15-28","title":"波峰餘高與牆頂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wave allowance and wall crest: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波峰餘高與牆頂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wave allowance and wall crest” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流。診斷時應採取以下查核：以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. Diagnose it by the following check: Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流。診斷時應採取以下查核：以高頻水位與影像核對最大浪峰是否集中於局部牆段，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. Diagnose it by the following check: Use rapid level records and imagery to locate concentrated wave crests along walls. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波峰餘高與牆頂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wave allowance and wall crest\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流。","排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets.","The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor"],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間平均水深會掩蓋短暫越頂噴流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Time-averaged depth conceals brief overtopping jets. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b247-v15-29","title":"底板排水與回水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Floor drainage and backwater: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「底板排水與回水」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Floor drainage and backwater” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側槽底板可能同時受地下水與表面變動壓力作用，排水出口若被下游水淹沒，原本自由排水條件會改變。淨水頭差應使用同時工況而非把不同洪水時刻的極值拼接；排水失效需與結構抗浮共同檢查。 驗證時應同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段，並辨識以下失效情境：下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「底板排水與回水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Groundwater and fluctuating surface pressure act on the floor together. A submerged drainage outlet changes the original free-drainage boundary. Use simultaneous states for differential head rather than combining incompatible extremes from different times, and evaluate drainage failure alongside structural uplift resistance. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Floor drainage and backwater” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「底板排水與回水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Floor drainage and backwater”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-29-k1","title":"底板排水與回水","titleEn":"Floor drainage and backwater","text":"側槽底板可能同時受地下水與表面變動壓力作用，排水出口若被下游水淹沒，原本自由排水條件會改變。淨水頭差應使用同時工況而非把不同洪水時刻的極值拼接；排水失效需與結構抗浮共同檢查。","textEn":"Groundwater and fluctuating surface pressure act on the floor together. A submerged drainage outlet changes the original free-drainage boundary.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「底板排水與回水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Floor drainage and backwater\" is correct?","options":["排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓","堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同","側槽底板可能同時受地下水與表面變動壓力作用，排水出口若被下游水淹沒，原本自由排水條件會改變。"],"optionsEn":["The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor","Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects","Groundwater and fluctuating surface pressure act on the floor together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"側槽底板可能同時受地下水與表面變動壓力作用，排水出口若被下游水淹沒，原本自由排水條件會改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Groundwater and fluctuating surface pressure act on the floor together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b247-v15-30","title":"底板排水與回水：定量估算","titleEn":"Floor drainage and backwater: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「底板排水與回水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Floor drainage and backwater” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「底板排水與回水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Floor drainage and backwater\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa。","側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同","側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa.","Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel","Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: underFloorHead=108 m; surfaceHead=105 m; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; netPressure=(108-105)*9.81=29.43 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b247-v15-31","title":"底板排水與回水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Floor drainage and backwater: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「底板排水與回水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Floor drainage and backwater” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「底板排水與回水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Floor drainage and backwater\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段。","出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods.","Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b247-v15-32","title":"底板排水與回水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Floor drainage and backwater: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「底板排水與回水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Floor drainage and backwater” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水孔存在就保證底板下沒有揚壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The presence of drains guarantees no pressure beneath the floor\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測底板上下水頭並檢查排水出口淹沒時段，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure heads above and below the floor together and identify outlet submergence periods. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底板排水與回水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Floor drainage and backwater\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同","下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects","Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"下游回水使排水反灌可升高底板下壓力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Downstream backwater can reverse drainage and raise subfloor pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b247-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「漂流木與有效堰長」與「模型守恆與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Debris and effective crest length\" and \"Model conservation and validation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b247-v15-33","title":"漂流木與有效堰長：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Debris and effective crest length: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「漂流木與有效堰長」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Debris and effective crest length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"漂流木可能卡在堰口與局部支柱，使有效堰長減少並改變側向入流分布。若暫時假設係數不變，可用堰長比估流量變化，但真實堵塞也會改變接近流與局部水頭；應以不同堵塞位置而非單一比例驗證。 驗證時應以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變，並辨識以下失效情境：相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漂流木與有效堰長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Debris can reduce effective crest length and redistribute lateral inflow. A length-ratio estimate holds the coefficient and head fixed, while real blockage also changes approach flow and local head. Test different blockage locations rather than assuming one percentage completely describes the hydraulic consequence. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Debris and effective crest length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75.","failure":"常見誤解：「堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漂流木與有效堰長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Debris and effective crest length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-33-k1","title":"漂流木與有效堰長","titleEn":"Debris and effective crest length","text":"漂流木可能卡在堰口與局部支柱，使有效堰長減少並改變側向入流分布。若暫時假設係數不變，可用堰長比估流量變化，但真實堵塞也會改變接近流與局部水頭；應以不同堵塞位置而非單一比例驗證。","textEn":"Debris can reduce effective crest length and redistribute lateral inflow. A length-ratio estimate holds the coefficient and head fixed, while real blockage also changes approach flow and local head.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漂流木與有效堰長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Debris and effective crest length\" is correct?","options":["漂流木可能卡在堰口與局部支柱，使有效堰長減少並改變側向入流分布。","堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同","水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確"],"optionsEn":["Debris can reduce effective crest length and redistribute lateral inflow.","Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects","Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漂流木可能卡在堰口與局部支柱，使有效堰長減少並改變側向入流分布。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Debris can reduce effective crest length and redistribute lateral inflow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b247-v15-34","title":"漂流木與有效堰長：定量估算","titleEn":"Debris and effective crest length: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漂流木與有效堰長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Debris and effective crest length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漂流木與有效堰長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Debris and effective crest length\", which statement holds?","options":["堰頂加長就一定可無限制增加整體洩量","原創教學假設：fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75。","連續方程單獨就能求出整條側槽水面線"],"optionsEn":["Lengthening the crest increases total system discharge without limit","Original teaching assumptions: fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75.","Continuity alone determines the complete side-channel water profile"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: fixedHeadAndCoefficient; clearLength=40 m; blockedLength=10 m; remainingCapacityFraction=(40-10)/40=0.75. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b247-v15-35","title":"漂流木與有效堰長：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Debris and effective crest length: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漂流木與有效堰長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Debris and effective crest length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漂流木與有效堰長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Debris and effective crest length\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","側槽同一斷面的水面必定完全水平","以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The water surface must be perfectly level across every side-channel section","Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b247-v15-36","title":"漂流木與有效堰長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Debris and effective crest length: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漂流木與有效堰長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Debris and effective crest length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水。診斷時應採取以下查核：以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. Diagnose it by the following check: Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「堵塞百分比相同就代表水力影響完全相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal blockage percentages always produce identical hydraulic effects\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水。診斷時應採取以下查核：以多種堵塞位置觀察槽內水位與入流分配改變，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. Diagnose it by the following check: Observe level and inflow redistribution for several debris-blockage locations. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漂流木與有效堰長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Debris and effective crest length\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確"],"optionsEn":["The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct"],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同堵塞比例位於出口附近可能造成更強局部回水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The same blockage fraction near the outlet can produce stronger local backwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b247-v15-37","title":"模型守恆與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Model conservation and validation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「模型守恆與驗證」如何影響側槽式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Model conservation and validation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Side-channel spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"三維側槽試驗或數值模型需同時通過水量平衡與水面線比較，單一出口流量吻合不代表流場正確。用控制體殘差可找出量測或網格問題，但小殘差也可能伴隨錯誤的紊流與邊界設定；應另比較局部波動與速度。 驗證時應核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線，並辨識以下失效情境：只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模型守恆與驗證」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A three-dimensional side-channel model needs both mass balance and profile validation. Matching outlet discharge does not prove the flow field. A control-volume residual flags measurement or discretization issues, but a small residual can coexist with wrong turbulence or boundaries; compare local velocities and fluctuations independently. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Model conservation and validation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模型守恆與驗證」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Model conservation and validation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-37-k1","title":"模型守恆與驗證","titleEn":"Model conservation and validation","text":"三維側槽試驗或數值模型需同時通過水量平衡與水面線比較，單一出口流量吻合不代表流場正確。用控制體殘差可找出量測或網格問題，但小殘差也可能伴隨錯誤的紊流與邊界設定；應另比較局部波動與速度。","textEn":"A three-dimensional side-channel model needs both mass balance and profile validation. Matching outlet discharge does not prove the flow field.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型守恆與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Model conservation and validation\" is correct?","options":["水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確","三維側槽試驗或數值模型需同時通過水量平衡與水面線比較，單一出口流量吻合不代表流場正確。","側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct","A three-dimensional side-channel model needs both mass balance and profile validation.","Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"三維側槽試驗或數值模型需同時通過水量平衡與水面線比較，單一出口流量吻合不代表流場正確。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A three-dimensional side-channel model needs both mass balance and profile validation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b247-v15-38","title":"模型守恆與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Model conservation and validation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模型守恆與驗證」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Model conservation and validation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模型守恆與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Model conservation and validation\", which statement holds?","options":["側向入流可當作早已沿槽流動的水量","出口控制只影響出口不會影響側槽上游","原創教學假設：MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent。"],"optionsEn":["Lateral inflow can be treated as water already moving along the channel","Outlet control affects only the outlet and never the upstream side channel","Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredInflow=100 m3/s; measuredOutflow=98 m3/s; steady residual=(100-98)/100*100=2 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b247-v15-39","title":"模型守恆與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Model conservation and validation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模型守恆與驗證」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Model conservation and validation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模型守恆與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Model conservation and validation\"?","options":["核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均水面低於牆頂就保證不會越流"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A mean water surface below the wall guarantees no overtopping"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b247-v15-40","title":"模型守恆與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Model conservation and validation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b247-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模型守恆與驗證」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Model conservation and validation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水量守恆通過就證明整個三維模型完全正確」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing mass balance proves that the entire three-dimensional model is correct\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b247-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對各入口總量與出口量並比較獨立水位測線，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile all inlet and outlet flows and compare independent water-level transects. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b247-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型守恆與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Model conservation and validation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布。","側槽上游與下游的流量永遠完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions.","Discharge is always identical upstream and downstream in a side channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只調參至流量守恆可能保留錯誤水面與流速分布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tuning only for mass balance can preserve incorrect water-level and velocity distributions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-fontenelle-model","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
